        <title type="html"><![CDATA[fix(html): add notes for dialog closedby=any touch propagation bug]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30834</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30834"/>
        <updated>2026-10-10T22:06:18.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185269030?u=1fc22565ccf4566b6f734fabaa87e03d9a31cfe4&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #30474.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5418797612" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30474" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30474/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30474">#30474</a></p>
<p dir="auto"><code class="notranslate">&lt;dialog closedby="any"&gt;</code> has a touch event propagation bug in Chrome 134–153<br>
and Firefox 141+: tapping the backdrop closes the dialog but does not cancel<br>
the event, causing click listeners on elements behind the backdrop to fire.</p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Changes:</strong></p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Chrome: converted to array — clean entry for 154+ (fixed via<br>
<a href="https://crbug.com/425579196" rel="nofollow">bug 425579196</a>), plus a 134–153 entry with a note</li>
<li>Firefox: added <code class="notranslate">notes</code> to the 141+ entry linking to<br>
<a href="https://bugzil.la/2022750" rel="nofollow">bug 2022750</a> (still unfixed as of Firefox 156)</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">chrome_android</code>, <code class="notranslate">edge</code>, and <code class="notranslate">firefox_android</code> correctly mirror their<br>
desktop entries — no additional changes needed</li>
</ul>]]></content>
