<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">From version 149, Chrome adds the ability for features of the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Payment_Request_API" rel="nofollow">Payment Request API</a>/ <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Web-Based_Payment_Handler_API" rel="nofollow">Web-based Payment Handler API</a> to reject with an <code class="notranslate">OperationError</code> to specifically indicate an internal error coming from the payment handler app, as opposed to user cancellation. See <a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5942637229113344" rel="nofollow">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5942637229113344</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">This is now true of the <code class="notranslate">PaymentRequest.show()</code> method and the <code class="notranslate">PaymentRequestEvent.respondWith()</code> method.</p>
<p dir="auto">This PR adds a data point for each of these.</p>

